{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/lineage_store.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:56:44.443350Z","id":"087058cc74ccdac30aa4d1a62cdb87868f22b1c7ec20613ed2657f115b7fb4a4","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-13-flutter-app-bundles-design.md §5.3 says an artifact_deleted event for <aid> removes its lineage entry and kept bundle, and §6.5 relies on it (deleting the app forgets the pin). The store offers forget(aid); the subscription to the daemon's events lives with the services or lib/app.dart, which must call it. Until then a deleted installed app's entry keeps matching its lineage in decide (lib/bundle/trust.dart), and a re-received bundle shows update/older/current against an app that no longer exists.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":284},"content_hash":"7097996b39736523795bed06ecf7cf492eff2b00bf0f23b15429ea069dfb98c5"},"summary":"Nothing calls LineageStore.forget on artifact_deleted yet","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
